Which direction the connection opens
On the left, the store, holding what is available to each participant and
opening nothing outward. On the right, three places that ask: one behind a
router with no public address, one offline for a weekend, and one belonging to
a rival organisation. Each asks what is available to it, takes it, and reports
back. Beneath, drawn faint, is what is therefore not needed: an address to
call, a hole in a firewall, a queue held open for a participant that is asleep,
or a retry schedule aimed at a building.
